    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110502" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φελλάτᾱς</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[λᾱ]</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">
			λίθος,</span> gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Polem.Hist.
			73
		</span></i>, ὁ:—a kind of <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>stone,</i> of which statues were
			made, <i><span class="en">
				Polem.Hist.
			</span></i> l.c., <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φελλεάτας</span></b> ,
			called 
				Dor.
			 and expld. by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κισσηρώδεις
			λίθοι</span> in Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				71
			</span></i> (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φελλέτας</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>); prob. the same as <i>pilates</i> and <i>pelastes</i>
			cited (acc. to codd.) fr. Cato by Fest.<i><span class="en">
				p.268L.
			</span></i> (Cf. sq.)</div>
